{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Patchset 2's fail-closed scan broke a precheck test; fixed structurally\n\n`make verify` on patchset 2 came back RC=2 with one failure:\n`tests/unit/test_close_duration_instrumentation.py::test_completion_precheck_threads_one_collector_through_pass_and_sidecar`.\n\n**Root cause — two of this patchset's own changes interacting.** The blocking-finding fix\nmakes `_refuse_open_sunset_marker` run unconditionally, so every precheck test now reaches\nthe marker scan. Advisory 1's fix made `_marker_lines` fail closed, but its benign branch\nmatched only the stderr text `not a git repository`. That test passes `/code`, a path that\ndoes not exist, and `git grep` reports a MISSING directory with the same exit status (128)\nand different prose:\n\n```\nfatal: cannot change to '/code': No such file or directory\n```\n\nso the scan raised `RuntimeError` and the precheck died.\n\n**The fix is structural, not a wider string match.** On an unexpected `git grep` status the\nscan now asks git whether a repository is reachable at all — a new `_has_repository` helper\nrunning `git -C <root> rev-parse --git-dir`. No repository means no tracked set, which is an\nempty answer; a repository that IS there and failed to scan still raises. Telling the two\napart by git's own structural answer rather than by its prose means a reworded or localized\nmessage cannot turn a failed scan into a silent pass, which was the whole point of advisory 1.\n\n**Test changes.**\n\n- New `test_a_code_root_that_does_not_exist_yields_no_markers` — the regression proof.\n  RED-proved: restoring the string-matching branch makes it fail with\n  `RuntimeError` at `sunset_markers.py:116`.\n- `test_a_failed_scan_raises_instead_of_passing_the_close` previously monkeypatched\n  `subprocess.run` to return 128 for EVERY call, which would now also fake away the\n  repository probe and let the guard excuse itself. Its fake now answers by argv:\n  `rev-parse` → 0, `grep` → 128. That is a more faithful model of the case it names — a real\n  repository whose grep failed — so the test actually exercises the raising path.\n\n`make lint` RC=0 (`active=647 new=32 increased=0 stale=0`, exit 0), `make typecheck` RC=0\nacross 754 source files, and the 30 tests across `test_sunset_markers.py`,\n`test_sunset_marker_close_gate_independence.py`, and `test_close_duration_instrumentation.py`\nall pass. Full `make verify` restarted.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793708444535182852,"uuid":"9bf948cd-f129-4f25-8f5c-637ad47f5a0e"}